+# ForkMesh product-contract evidence
+
+This map records the evidence behind each product-contract claim and distinguishes working product actions, automated coverage, operator proof that still needs to be captured, and roadmap work.
+It must be updated when a claim, route, or evidence source changes.
+
+## Evidence statuses
+
+- **Working product action** means a user can take the linked action in the current product.
+- **Automated coverage** means the linked test exercises the stated behavior, but is not proof of a production deployment.
+- **Operator proof required** means an operator must capture the live result before the claim is presented as fully closed in production.
+- **Roadmap** means the capability or its evidence is not complete and must not be represented as live.
+
+## Claim-to-evidence map
+
+| Claim | Status | Product action and evidence |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Collaborate | Working product action and Automated coverage | Open [issues](/docs/#issues), [pull requests](/docs/#pull-requests), or [encrypted rooms](/docs/#chat) on a ForkMesh repository. The public proof path links to these actions and is covered by [test_product_proof_path.py](../cloudflare_worker/tests/test_product_proof_path.py). |
+| Mirror | Working product action and Automated coverage | [Install a desktop node](/desktop), publish or mirror a repository, then open Repositories and select that repository before opening its Mirrors tab at [/dashboard/repos](/dashboard/repos). The documented route is covered by [test_product_proof_path.py](../cloudflare_worker/tests/test_product_proof_path.py). |
+| Preserve | Automated coverage and Operator proof required | Follow the [mirror failover guidance](/docs/#mirror-failover) and clone from the same repository URL after a source host is unavailable. [test_mirror_failover_chaos.py](../cloudflare_worker/tests/test_mirror_failover_chaos.py) and [test_clone_fallback.py](../cloudflare_worker/tests/test_clone_fallback.py) cover the fallback behavior. Capture an operator run as live production evidence before describing this path as fully proven. |
+| Independent hosts | Working product action and Automated coverage | The [repository model](/docs/#repository), [host tunnel](/docs/#host-tunnel), and [self-hosting guide](/docs/#self-hosting) describe local desktop nodes and relay boundaries. The local-node behavior is exercised by [test_mirror_failover_chaos.py](../cloudflare_worker/tests/test_mirror_failover_chaos.py). |
+| No single hosting provider | Working product action and Operator proof required | The Worker coordinates discovery and routing but is **not canonical Git storage**. The [repository model](/docs/#repository) and [self-hosting guide](/docs/#self-hosting) describe the boundary. Record a live multi-host operator proof before treating provider independence as production-closed. |
+| Supported platforms | Working product action and Automated coverage | The [desktop install page](/desktop) lists supported installers. [test_installer_diag.py](../cloudflare_worker/tests/test_installer_diag.py) covers anonymous installer diagnostics and [test_install_diag.py](../cloudflare_worker/tests/test_install_diag.py) covers validation for the install diagnostic route. |
+| Failure paths | Automated coverage and Operator proof required | [Mirror failover guidance](/docs/#mirror-failover) explains the source-unavailable check. [test_mirror_failover_chaos.py](../cloudflare_worker/tests/test_mirror_failover_chaos.py) covers failure and recovery behavior. An operator must retain a real failover run for production proof. |
+| Rollback and recovery | Roadmap | Publish an operator recovery runbook with rollback decisions, ownership, and recovery-time evidence. Add a repeatable recovery test before making a completed recovery claim. |
+| Telemetry and measurement | Working product action, Automated coverage, and Roadmap | Public pages collect only the allowlisted `forkmesh.homepage_cta_clicked`, `forkmesh.install_command_copied`, and `forkmesh.proof_path_link_clicked` interactions. [test_product_telemetry.py](../cloudflare_worker/tests/test_product_telemetry.py), [test_telemetry.py](../cloudflare_worker/tests/test_telemetry.py), [test_installer_diag.py](../cloudflare_worker/tests/test_installer_diag.py), and [test_status_page.py](../cloudflare_worker/tests/test_status_page.py) cover the controls and existing diagnostics. `forkmesh.desktop_installer_started`, `forkmesh.desktop_installer_succeeded`, `forkmesh.repo_mirrored_or_published`, `forkmesh.clone_route_requested`, and `forkmesh.clone_fallback_served_by_mirror` remain Roadmap until a privacy-reviewed aggregate can collect them without repository, user, host, or clone URL data. |
+| Documentation | Working product action and Automated coverage | The public [docs landing page](/docs/) and its [proof path](/docs/#proof-path) are covered by [test_docs_frontend.py](../cloudflare_worker/tests/test_docs_frontend.py) and [test_product_proof_path.py](../cloudflare_worker/tests/test_product_proof_path.py). |
+
+## Closure record
+
+Attach the date, environment, anonymized result, and responsible operator when an Operator proof required item is completed.
+Do not replace a product action or production proof with a test-only claim.
+Do not promote a Roadmap item until its linked action, evidence, and operating guidance are complete.
+
+## Measurement definitions
+
+- Promise comprehension is the percentage of participants who pass the [comprehension template](research/product-promise-comprehension-template.md) for each five-person cohort.
+- Homepage-to-clone conversion begins with `forkmesh.homepage_cta_clicked` and requires the Roadmap `forkmesh.clone_route_requested` aggregate before it can be calculated end to end.
+- Unsupported-claim count is the number of failures in [test_product_contract_copy.py](../cloudflare_worker/tests/test_product_contract_copy.py) and should remain zero on every change.
