+# Canonical Product Promise Design
+
+## Goal
+
+Make the approved ForkMesh product promise the first positioning sentence across the public entry points named in the issue.
+
+## Canonical promise
+
+> ForkMesh lets developers collaborate on, mirror, and preserve source-code repositories across independent hosts—without relying on any single hosting provider.
+
+## Scope
+
+The root `README.md` remains the source reference and is not edited.
+
+The homepage uses the promise in its hero description, standard metadata, social metadata, and applicable JSON-LD descriptions.
+
+The repository page uses the promise in its static page metadata without changing repository-specific interface behavior.
+
+The signup, desktop, pricing, and mirror-payouts pages use the promise as their first visible positioning sentence and retain their present feature-specific details afterward.
+
+Both documentation entry points, `public/docs.html` and `public/docs/index.html`, use the promise in their metadata and opening lead copy.
+
+## Content rules
+
+The promise must be reproduced verbatim, including its punctuation.
+
+Existing copy about live mirrors, signed collaboration, encrypted rooms, AI agents, pricing, bounties, and operator rewards remains after the promise as supporting detail.
+
+Existing headlines and task-oriented page copy remain unless they prevent the canonical promise from being the first explanatory product-positioning sentence.
+
+## Verification
+
+A focused static test will require the exact promise in every target HTML page and the homepage metadata and structured data surfaces.
+
+Existing page-specific static tests will be run to ensure that the targeted pages retain their required UI contracts.
